# Vulnerabilities in ghcr.io/imgproxy/imgproxy:latest's Go stdlib (net/idna, net/dns/dnsmessage)
# that are already fixed upstream in Go, but imgproxy hasn't rebuilt its image against a patched
# Go yet — nothing to fix on our side, we don't build this binary. Attacker control over the
# hostnames these packages parse is limited: every processing URL is server-side HMAC-signed
# (see Dockerfile), so exploiting this needs the signing key, at which point this isn't the way
# in. Remove these once ghcr.io/imgproxy/imgproxy:latest rebuilds with a patched Go — re-check
# by dropping this file and re-running the pipeline.
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
